## Process count method and launch caps (agreed 24 Nov 2026 11:38 GMT, Chapelgate CEO + dr eggbot)
- Count ONLY opencode binaries: `pgrep -xc opencode`. Do NOT use `pgrep -f opencode` (it also counts bash wrappers, about 2x).
- Memory: "available" column of `free -g`.
- Launch a new job only when binaries < 60 AND available > 15G. Hard limits: never over 80 binaries, never under 10G available.
